rse impact on our business.","context":"•repayment of our debt may require a significant amount of cash, and we may not have sufficient cash flow from our business or the ability to raise funds to pay our substantial debt; and","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":653,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}},{"id":"63a2012745e541f0977bc894a8b8afdf6b5a39c1d9ccb1dcb6e59d3dd16c90c3","quote":"We have a history of losses and may not be able to achieve or sustain profitability in the future.","context":"Risks Related to Our Growth","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":656,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}},{"id":"8c4ee208f195581858d68a63ac99ddb46ea4132f1bdd724c95e5e34cf284a56e","quote":"We have incurred net losses in all annual periods since our inception, and we expect we will continue to incur net losses for the foreseeable future. We experienced net losses of $41.5 million, $57.7 million and $202.3 million for fiscal 2025, fiscal 2024 and fiscal 2023, respectively. As of April 30, 2026, we had an accumulated deficit of $1,249.4 million. Because the market for our cloud platform is rapidly evolving and cloud-based security solutions are still in the process of being widely adopted, it is difficult for us to predict our future results of operations. We expect our operating expenses to increase significantly over the next several years as we continue to hire additional personnel, particularly in research and development and sales and marketing, expand our operations and infrastructure, both domestically and internationally, and continue to develop our platform. If we fail to increase our revenue to offset the increases in our operating expenses, we may not achieve or sustain profitability in the future.","context":"We have a history of losses and may not be able to achieve or sustain profitability in the future.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":657,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}},{"id":"e92839f5faeb3514843cfccb1349c0668ea60f2d78ec8290f5b5e31c9faebad8","quote":"Additionally, our business strategy continues to focus primarily on long-term growth. As we execute on this strategy, we may ultimately be unable to achieve or sustain profitability at the level contemplated by industry or financial analysts and our stockholders, or at all, and as a result, our stock price may decline.","context":"We have incurred net losses in all annual periods since our inception, and we expect we will continue to incur net losses for the foreseeable future. We experienced net losses of $41.5 million, $57.7 million and $202.3 million for fiscal 2025, fiscal 2024 and fiscal 2023, respectively. As of April 30, 2026, we had an accumulated deficit of $1,249.4 million. Because the market for our cloud platform is rapidly evolving and cloud-based security solutions are still in the process of being widely adopted, it is difficult for us to predict our future results of operations. We expect our operating expenses to increase significantly over the next several years as we continue to hire additional personnel, particularly in research and development and sales and marketing, expand our operations and infrastructure, both domestically and internationally, and continue to develop our platform. If we fail to increase our revenue to offset the increases in our operating expenses, we may not achieve or sustain profitability in the future.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":658,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}},{"id":"5634ba32534c6a707a8a19c64998bf492d2a7bc3712dad55235920be35428bc9","quote":"If organizations do not adopt our cloud platform, our ability to grow our business and operating results may be adversely affected.","context":"Additionally, our business strategy continues to focus primarily on long-term growth. As we execute on this strategy, we may ultimately be unable to achieve or sustain profitability at the level contemplated by industry or financial analysts and our stockholders, or at all, and as a result, our stock price may decline.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":659,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}},{"id":"3ce2c9d48eba959f93879e300bf8a151727798019df66e93fca543c2099cb779","quote":"Cloud security technologies are still evolving, and it remains difficult to predict customer demand and adoption rates for our solutions. We believe that our cloud platform offers superior protection to our customers, who are moving their applications and data to the cloud and embracing AI applications and agents. We also believe that our cloud platform represents a major shift from on-premises appliance-based security solutions. While cloud-based security solutions have seen increased adoption, traditional on-premises security appliances continue to be entrenched in the infrastructure of many of our potential customers, particularly large enterprises, because of their prior investment in and the familiarity of their IT personnel with on-premises appliance-based solutions. As a result, our sales process often involves extensive efforts to educate our customers on the benefits and capabilities of our cloud platform, particularly as we continue to pursue customer","context":"If organizations do not adopt our cloud platform, our ability to grow our business and operating results may be adversely affected.","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":660,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}},{"id":"6a9c648853888bd8baa3521622e98eaae3ea19e085c088fabbbfbfb0d24481ec","quote":"relationships with large organizations. Even with these efforts, we cannot predict long-term market acceptance of our cloud platform, or the adoption of competing products, services or technologies. If we fail to achieve or maintain broad market acceptance of our cloud platform or are unable to keep pace with industry changes, particularly as a result of AI, our ability to grow our business and our operating results will be materially and adversely affected.","context":"Table of Contents","section":"Item 1A. Risk Factors","block":663,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}}],"omittedEvidenceCount":0},"segmentIntelligence":{"status":"evidence_available","evidence":[{"id":"bc3cea0131abdd8da1bd88e058f3e6d52d674854d34cdb51dcb59b21a96ebdfb","quote":"In November 2024, the FASB issued ASU No. 2024-03, Income Statement - Reporting Comprehensive Income - Expense Disaggregation Disclosures (Subtopic 220-40), Disaggregation of Income Statement Expenses. This standard requires disclosures of additional information about specific expense categories in the notes to the financial statements for","context":"In July 2025, the FASB issued ASU No. 2025-05, Financial Instruments-Credit Losses (Topic 326): Measurement of Credit Losses for Accounts Receivable and Contract Assets. This standard amends guidance on measuring expected credit losses for current accounts receivable and contract assets arising from revenue contracts. The amended guidance requires estimation of credit losses for these short-term assets based on the economic conditions that exist as of the balance sheet date, without forecasting future economic conditions. This standard is effective for us in the annual and interim periods beginning in the first quarter of fiscal 2027. We are currently evaluating the potential impact of this standard on our consolidated financial statement disclosures.","section":"Item 1. Financial Statements","block":146,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c"}},{"id":"be500a90684b17f054a5cde8dded88051a366e2e1d43187f12e2de519285eab7","quote":"10","context":"In November 2024, the FASB issued ASU No. 2024-03, Income Statement - Reporting Comprehensive Income - Expense Disaggregation Disclosures (Subtopic 220-40), Disaggregation of Income Statement Expenses. This standard requires disclosures of additional information about specific expense categories in the notes to the financial statements for","section":"Item 1. Financial Statements","block":147,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001713683-26-000096","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-05-26","reportDate":"2026-04-30","cik":"0001713683","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1713683/000171368326000096/zs-20260430.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/df05f5637b8ba9dc2efec2b4e12924de5b2f50606a469f26bbab4c509642fb2c.bin","sha256":"df05f5637b8